;; Written by Claude, 2026-10-13, for Phase 17 step 3 (design section
;; 19.9, proposal 2, approved by the user); reviewed by the user,
;; 2026-10-13. It replaces the file the user reviewed on 2026-10-13. Why
;; this is right:
;; - Err now imports FormattedOutput, not FormattedText, and calls it
;;   for everything but IsConsole, as on LLVM; its own Field is gone. Its
;;   initializer calls LINEOUTPUT_INIT, then FORMATTEDOUTPUT_INIT, then
;;   FindConsole.
;; - Each of Char, String, Ln, Int, Hex, Real and LongReal passes its
;;   stream, LineOutput.error (MOVL #1), as the first argument, then its own
;;   parameters as before: CHAR and INTEGER as longwords, the open array
;;   as address and length, a HUGEINT as the address of a quadword copy,
;;   a REAL by value (MOVF), a LONGREAL as the address of a copy (MOVG).
;; - Ten passes e as a longword to FORMATTEDOUTPUT_TEN and returns its
;;   G_floating result in R0 and R1; a function that reached its END
;;   would trap (12).
;; - IsConsole is an exported BOOLEAN ("::"). FindConsole copies
;;   "SYS$ERROR" (MOVC5, 9 bytes, zero-filled to 16) and calls
;;   POC_IS_TERMINAL, Platform's routine ($GETDVIW, DVI$_DEVCLASS
;;   DC$_TERM), with its address and length 9, and sets IsConsole when
;;   R0 is 1. Unchanged.
;; - Err's key is new: its interface is the same, but its symbol file
;;   lists its imports, now FormattedOutput and LineOutput.
;; - On the guest every fixture that prints through Err prints what it
;;   printed before.
